A company careers page ({{ url }}) was opened in a browser and draws its job list with
JavaScript. Below is what the page offered. Choose ONE way to read the full list of jobs; our
code will then run your choice. You do not read or return the jobs yourself.

Methods:
- "json_ld": the page has schema.org JobPosting data (only if listed below).
- "api_response": one of the JSON responses the page loaded. Set `api_url` to one of the listed
  response URLs, copied exactly. `items_path` is the dotted path to the array of jobs ("" when the
  document itself is the array). `fields` maps title, url, location, posted and description to
  dotted paths inside one item; title and url are required, the others only when the item has them.
- "css": CSS selectors on the rendered page. `css.item` selects one block per job (use a listed
  selector, or a more specific one); title, link, location and posted are selectors relative to
  one item. `link` must point at the job's own page.

Prefer the method whose list is complete and has real job titles and links. You may also fill in
the parameters of a second method as a fallback. Do not invent URLs or fields that are not shown.
